{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.PrintWriter;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        int n = in.nextInt();\n        if (n > 40) {\n            out.println(0);\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n\n        ArrayList<Point> points = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            points.add(new Point(in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt()));\n        }\n\n        if (n < 3) {\n            out.println(n);\n            for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) out.println(i);\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n\n        ArrayList<Integer> answer = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int center = 0; center < n; ++center) {\n            Point c = points.get(center);\n            boolean good = true;\n\n            for (int a = 0; a < n && good; ++a) {\n                if (a == center) continue;\n                for (int b = a + 1; b < n; ++b) {\n                    if (b == center) continue;\n                    if (hasAcute(c, points.get(a), points.get(b))) {\n                        good = false;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (good) answer.add(center + 1);\n        }\n\n        out.println(answer.size());\n        for (int id : answer) out.println(id);\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static boolean hasAcute(Point c, Point x, Point y) {\n        long dx1 = x.a - c.a;\n        long dy1 = x.b - c.b;\n        long dz1 = x.c - c.c;\n        long du1 = x.d - c.d;\n        long dv1 = x.e - c.e;\n\n        long dx2 = y.a - c.a;\n        long dy2 = y.b - c.b;\n        long dz2 = y.c - c.c;\n        long du2 = y.d - c.d;\n        long dv2 = y.e - c.e;\n\n        return dx1 * dx2 + dy1 * dy2 + dz1 * dz2 + du1 * du2 + dv1 * dv2 > 0;\n    }\n\n    static class Point {\n        long a, b, c, d, e;\n\n        Point(long a, long b, long c, long d, long e) {\n            this.a = a;\n            this.b = b;\n            this.c = c;\n            this.d = d;\n            this.e = e;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Point {\n    long long a, b, c, d, e;\n    Point(long long a, long long b, long long c, long long d, long long e) : a(a), b(b), c(c), d(d), e(e) {}\n};\n\nbool hasAcute(const Point& c, const Point& x, const Point& y) {\n    long long dx1 = x.a - c.a;\n    long long dy1 = x.b - c.b;\n    long long dz1 = x.c - c.c;\n    long long du1 = x.d - c.d;\n    long long dv1 = x.e - c.e;\n\n    long long dx2 = y.a - c.a;\n    long long dy2 = y.b - c.b;\n    long long dz2 = y.c - c.c;\n    long long du2 = y.d - c.d;\n    long long dv2 = y.e - c.e;\n\n    return dx1 * dx2 + dy1 * dy2 + dz1 * dz2 + du1 * du2 + dv1 * dv2 > 0;\n}\